---
import Layout from '../../layouts/CommercialLayout.astro';
import EnergyScene from '../../components/illustrations/EnergyScene.astro';
import DayTimeline from '../../components/illustrations/DayTimeline.astro';
import SectorScene from '../../components/illustrations/SectorScene.astro';
---
<Layout lang="en" page="home" title="Smart charging and energy management for your site" description="Charge more vehicles within your existing grid connection. Stroomlijnen connects smart charging, solar and storage in one energy management system." showClosing={false}>
 <div class="home-story">
  <section class="story-hero shell" aria-labelledby="home-title">
   <div class="story-hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Smart charging · energy management</p>
    <h1 id="home-title">Your business grows.<br/><em>So does demand.</em></h1>
    <p class="story-intro">More electric vehicles, the same grid connection. Smart charging and energy management from Stroomlijnen keep capacity available for your business and help you control energy costs.</p>
    <a class="button" href="/en/contact/">Discuss your site <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    <a class="story-scroll" href="#werkdag"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span> Discover how it works</a>
   </div>
   <figure class="story-hero-image site-illustration">
    <EnergyScene variant="hero" lang="en"/>
    <figcaption><span>Your site as one energy system</span><span>Simplified illustration</span></figcaption>
   </figure>
  </section>
  <nav class="story-chapters shell" aria-label="From your working day to a charging plan that fits"><a href="#werkdag">01 / Your working day</a><a href="#energie">02 / Room to charge</a><a href="#sectoren">03 / Your site</a></nav>

  <section id="werkdag" class="story-problem shell story-section" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
   <div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Your working day</p><h2 id="problem-title">Everything comes together.<br/>On one grid connection.</h2><p class="story-intro">Your vehicles need to charge while your business needs power. But your grid connection is limited and upgrading it is expensive. Energy prices fluctuate, and solar goes unused when generation and demand do not align.</p></div>
   <DayTimeline lang="en"/>
   <div class="story-day">
    <p class="story-small-label">What a working day could look like</p>
    <ol>
     <li><time>08:00</time><div><h3>Vehicles arrive</h3><p>The first vehicles plug in as the building starts up.</p></div></li>
     <li><time>11:00</time><div><h3>Business is busy</h3><p>The kitchen, climate control or production needs power; charging adapts.</p></div></li>
     <li><time>14:00</time><div><h3>Room to charge</h3><p>Solar power goes to vehicles that will stay a little longer.</p></div></li>
     <li><time>22:00</time><div><h3>Ready for tomorrow</h3><p>If the tariff is favourable, the remaining vehicles charge before their next trip.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="story-fine">An illustrative working day, not measured data.</p>
   </div>
  </section>

  <section id="energie" class="story-energy" aria-labelledby="energy-title">
   <div class="shell story-section">
    <div class="story-energy-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / Room to charge</p><h2 id="energy-title">Charging, solar and storage.<br/><em>Managed together.</em></h2></div><p>The Stroomlijnen energy management system (EMS) coordinates your chargers with the building, solar generation and battery storage where available. It keeps your site within the agreed connection limit and works to lower energy costs. One platform, one dashboard, one partner.</p></div>
    <figure class="story-flow">
     <EnergyScene variant="wide" lang="en"/>
     <EnergyScene variant="compact" lang="en"/>
     <figcaption><span>Simply put: available power is shared between your building and chargers.</span><span>Simplified illustration · possibilities vary by site</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ol class="story-steps">
     <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Stay within your connection</h3><p>The EMS allocates available power. When demand in your building rises, vehicles temporarily charge more slowly.</p></div></li>
     <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Use more of your solar</h3><p>Charge vehicles when your panels are generating. A battery lets you save surplus energy for later.</p></div></li>
     <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Charge at favourable times</h3><p>Departure times and energy tariffs help determine when to charge. You can see consumption and charging sessions in one dashboard.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
   </div>
  </section>

  <section id="sectoren" class="story-applications" aria-labelledby="applications-title">
   <div class="shell story-section">
    <div class="story-app-intro"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Your site</p><h2 id="applications-title">Your industry.<br/>Your working day.</h2><p>A hotel has different peaks from a distribution centre. We tailor power allocation to your site, vehicles and operations.</p></div>
    <div class="story-application-list">
     <a href="/en/contact/"><SectorScene sector="hospitality"/><div><h3>Hospitality</h3><p>Guests charge during their stay while the kitchen and climate control retain enough power.</p><span class="story-application-link">Discuss your site</span></div><span class="story-application-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
     <a href="/en/contact/"><SectorScene sector="transport"/><div><h3>Transport & logistics</h3><p>Your fleet charges within available capacity, timed around its next departures.</p><span class="story-application-link">Discuss your site</span></div><span class="story-application-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
     <a href="/en/contact/"><SectorScene sector="property"/><div><h3>Property & facilities</h3><p>You share power between tenants, building systems and chargers at the same site.</p><span class="story-application-link">Discuss your site</span></div><span class="story-application-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
     <a href="/en/contact/"><SectorScene sector="industry"/><div><h3>Industry</h3><p>Charging and battery storage adapt to your production peaks and solar generation.</p><span class="story-application-link">Discuss your site</span></div><span class="story-application-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <details class="story-kit"><summary>The charger follows your working day <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="story-kit-body"><dl><div><dt>Fixed DC charger</dt><dd><strong>120 kW</strong><p>Expandable to 160 kW with an additional 40 kW module.</p></dd></div><div><dt>AC · longer stays</dt><dd><strong>22 kW</strong></dd></div><div><dt>Mobile DC · on site</dt><dd><strong>30 kW</strong></dd></div></dl><p>Vehicle recognition via EVCCID/MAC, where supported by the vehicle and charger.</p><p class="story-fine">Nominal ratings. Actual charging power depends on the vehicle and site.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://docs.stroomlijnen.nl/en/">Explore our documentation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></details>
   </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-contact shell story-section" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
   <div><p class="eyebrow">The next step starts with a conversation</p><h2 id="contact-title">More charging.<br/><em>What can your site do?</em></h2></div>
   <div class="story-contact-copy"><svg class="contact-mark" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M50 91S17 62 17 37a33 33 0 0 1 66 0C83 62 50 91 50 91Z" fill="#0C2340"/><circle cx="50" cy="37" r="19" fill="none" stroke="#00B0E4" stroke-width="7"/><path d="M50 18a19 19 0 0 1 19 19" fill="none" stroke="#84BD00" stroke-width="7"/></svg><p>Tell us about your connection, vehicles and energy use. Together, we will explore where smart charging, solar and storage can free up capacity and reduce costs.</p><a class="button" href="/en/contact/">Discuss your site <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="story-docs"><p>Want the technical details?</p><a class="text-link" href="https://docs.stroomlijnen.nl/en/">Explore our documentation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
  </section>
 </div>
</Layout>
<script>
 import '../../scripts/home-story';
</script>

<style>
 .story-hero h1 { width:100%; font-size:clamp(2.8rem,4.7vw,4.6rem); }
 @media(max-width:760px) {
  .story-hero h1 { font-size:clamp(2.5rem,8vw,4rem); }
 }
</style>
